12. How to explain your real-time project experience in an interview
This is important. At 6 years of experience, don't just explain commands. Explain how you used them in your project.

You can use this sample answer as a template, adjusting it to your actual experience.

Question: Explain your Git and GitHub workflow in your current project.

Sample interview answer:

"In my project, we use GitHub as our source code management platform.

We maintain separate branches for development, release and production. Developers create individual feature branches from the development branch and work on their assigned tasks.

After completing the changes, they commit and push the code to GitHub and create a Pull Request.

We have configured branch protection rules, which require peer reviews and successful CI pipeline execution before merging.

When a PR is created, our CI pipeline performs code checkout, compilation, unit testing, SonarQube analysis and security scanning.

After approval, the PR is merged into the development branch.

Once the release is ready, we promote the changes through the release and production process. Our CI/CD pipeline builds Docker images, pushes them to Amazon ECR and deploys the application to ECS or EKS, depending on the application.

We also use Git tags to identify releases and Git revert to safely roll back problematic code changes.

I am also involved in troubleshooting merge conflicts, failed pipeline executions, incorrect branch merges and production deployment issues."

